1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kisskh.club =

2
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,059
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:01,059 --> 00:00:02,059
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:02,059 --> 00:00:03,626
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:07,426 --> 00:00:13,311
[Winter, 2011]

6
00:00:13,311 --> 00:00:17,883
Come on, I told you to order something
expensive. Get some boiled pork too.

7
00:00:17,883 --> 00:00:19,467
You're a college student.
How much money could you have?

8
00:00:19,467 --> 00:00:21,455
It's fine. This is enough.

9
00:00:21,455 --> 00:00:23,727
I work part-time.

10
00:00:23,727 --> 00:00:25,295
I have more money than you.

11
00:00:25,295 --> 00:00:27,503
How? You're just
a civil service exam student.

12
00:00:27,503 --> 00:00:29,226
My mom.

13
00:00:29,979 --> 00:00:32,326
She's been saving up more than I realized.

14
00:00:35,491 --> 00:00:37,619
Is studying for the police exam going okay?

15
00:00:37,619 --> 00:00:38,983
I guess it's just right for me.

16
00:00:38,983 --> 00:00:40,355
It really sticks in my head.

17
00:00:40,355 --> 00:00:41,779
Just wait and see.

18
00:00:41,779 --> 00:00:46,611
I'll be wearing a badge within two years,
and I'll catch that punk myself.

19
00:00:46,611 --> 00:00:48,603
And then what, after you catch him?

20
00:00:48,603 --> 00:00:50,151
After that?

21
00:00:50,151 --> 00:00:51,419
Then I'll catch the next punk.

22
00:00:51,419 --> 00:00:53,159
Jeez, forget it, you punk.

23
00:00:53,791 --> 00:00:56,792
You talked me into being a reporter,
and now you're betraying me.

24
00:00:56,792 --> 00:00:58,192
The more I think about it,
the more pissed off I get.

25
00:00:58,192 --> 00:01:01,727
Hey, if we're all digging,
who's going to catch the fish?

26
00:01:01,727 --> 00:01:03,411
You just keep digging.

27
00:01:03,411 --> 00:01:05,167
I'll catch the fish.

28
00:01:05,167 --> 00:01:07,647
You do your job, and I'll do mine.

29
00:01:07,647 --> 00:01:09,179
Bang, bang!

30
00:01:09,179 --> 00:01:10,287
Oh, please.

31
00:01:10,287 --> 00:01:12,747
Don't get beaten to a pulp
by some criminal later.

32
00:01:12,747 --> 00:01:15,731
- Ma'am, could you turn up the TV?
- Sure.

33
00:01:15,731 --> 00:01:18,212
[Police Focused on Kingfisher Investigation]
The shooting incidents

34
00:01:18,212 --> 00:01:22,143
by the serial killer known as Kingfisher
have risen to nine.

35
00:01:22,143 --> 00:01:25,563
Police have concluded that
last week's shooting in Cheongsin-dong

36
00:01:25,563 --> 00:01:27,599
[Kingfisher Shootings Rise to 9]
was also the work of the same suspect.

37
00:01:27,599 --> 00:01:30,426
[Cheongsin-dong Case Also Same Culprit]
They are intensifying their investigation.

38
00:01:30,426 --> 00:01:34,451
Meanwhile, the number of members
in an online Kingfisher fan club

39
00:01:34,451 --> 00:01:36,079
- is approaching 300,000...
- A fan club?

40
00:01:36,079 --> 00:01:37,726
Have they all lost their darn minds?

41
00:01:37,726 --> 00:01:39,626
Why are they cheering for that lunatic?

42
00:01:39,626 --> 00:01:42,063
Maybe they get
some kind of catharsis from it.

43
00:01:42,063 --> 00:01:44,692
He picks out the worst criminals
and kills them.

44
00:01:44,692 --> 00:01:45,759
Catharsis, my foot.

45
00:01:45,759 --> 00:01:50,115
Hey, isn't killing a murderer still murder?

46
00:01:50,115 --> 00:01:52,363
Even if he only kills criminals for now,

47
00:01:52,363 --> 00:01:54,826
who's to say he won't kill
an innocent person someday?

48
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:59,692
If, by chance, I mean, seriously, what if...

49
00:02:01,551 --> 00:02:04,291
just hypothetically,
Kingfisher killed that punk...

50
00:02:04,291 --> 00:02:06,226
That punk? Who...

51
00:02:08,592 --> 00:02:11,875
Do you really think
I'd feel happy or thankful?

52
00:02:11,875 --> 00:02:14,559
I mean, he'd be taking revenge
for you, or something like that.

53
00:02:14,559 --> 00:02:16,619
Darn it. Hey!

54
00:02:16,619 --> 00:02:20,287
If another murderer kills
my parents' murderer, is that revenge?

55
00:02:20,287 --> 00:02:22,091
If anyone's going to take revenge,
it should be me.

56
00:02:22,091 --> 00:02:24,259
What right does Kingfisher have?

57
00:02:30,139 --> 00:02:32,426
My revenge is

58
00:02:32,426 --> 00:02:36,159
to catch him and put him
in prison for the rest of his life.

59
00:02:36,159 --> 00:02:39,119
To me, they're both the same murdering punk.

60
00:02:39,119 --> 00:02:41,651
Once I catch that punk,

61
00:02:41,651 --> 00:02:45,992
I'll catch Kingfisher next, no matter what.

62
00:02:46,895 --> 00:02:49,143
Just wait and see.

63
00:02:49,143 --> 00:02:50,843
Alright.

64
00:02:55,192 --> 00:02:56,319
Oh, my.

65
00:02:56,319 --> 00:02:59,215
Oh, my, I'm so sorry.

66
00:02:59,215 --> 00:03:02,399
Ma'am, one plate of boiled pork, please.

67
00:03:02,399 --> 00:03:03,819
To cover the dry cleaning.

68
00:03:03,819 --> 00:03:06,526
Keep your strength up, future detective.

69
00:03:08,143 --> 00:03:10,659
Thirty thousand won,
including the boiled pork? Alright.

70
00:03:10,659 --> 00:03:12,359
What's with her?

71
00:03:19,226 --> 00:03:22,259
[Episode 10]

72
00:03:22,259 --> 00:03:24,259
[Client Suitability Assessment,
One-Month Post-Release Observation]

73
00:03:24,259 --> 00:03:26,389
[Multiple Risk Indicators,
High Reoffending Risk]

74
00:03:34,411 --> 00:03:37,592
Why? Because of the victim's son who's a cop?

75
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:46,019
I thought he looked familiar. Now I remember.

76
00:03:46,019 --> 00:03:51,219
I saw him in the first-floor lobby
when we were leaving your housewarming party.

77
00:03:51,219 --> 00:03:53,395
I've heard about it.

78
00:03:53,395 --> 00:03:55,171
He's a friend of my husband's.

79
00:03:55,171 --> 00:03:56,455
Yeah?

80
00:03:56,455 --> 00:03:58,155
Your husband...

81
00:03:59,179 --> 00:04:01,526
had a friend like that?

82
00:04:02,219 --> 00:04:07,326
If you're really uncomfortable with it,
let's change the scenario.

83
00:04:13,526 --> 00:04:16,375
Why do people never really change?

84
00:04:16,375 --> 00:04:19,043
Twenty years is a pretty long time.

85
00:04:19,043 --> 00:04:20,743
Exactly.

86
00:04:21,711 --> 00:04:23,859
They commit sins
that even repentance and remorse

87
00:04:23,859 --> 00:04:26,839
can never make the victims' families forgive.

88
00:04:26,839 --> 00:04:28,491
Why do they even do it?

89
00:04:28,491 --> 00:04:30,226
At times like this,

90
00:04:30,859 --> 00:04:36,359
that saying, "A leopard can't change
its spots," feels so cruel, doesn't it?

91
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:40,595
But still, not everyone kills just because

92
00:04:40,595 --> 00:04:42,926
they grew up in different
conditions and environments.

93
00:04:42,926 --> 00:04:49,402
Plenty of people serve the time they deserve
and then go on to live new lives.

94
00:04:50,159 --> 00:04:54,326
That's why the law and the state
give them another chance.

95
00:04:57,943 --> 00:05:00,126
Let's stick to the scenario.

96
00:05:00,823 --> 00:05:02,526
Will you be okay?

97
00:05:03,209 --> 00:05:04,209
I have to be.

98
00:05:04,209 --> 00:05:08,392
It's my job, and it's what I can do.

99
00:05:21,335 --> 00:05:23,026
Why are you going after that punk, you idiot?

100
00:05:23,026 --> 00:05:25,959
What are you planning to do if you meet him?

101
00:05:26,707 --> 00:05:29,675
What do you mean? I'm just watching him.

102
00:05:29,675 --> 00:05:31,323
Why? What...

103
00:05:31,323 --> 00:05:33,359
Worried the cop might do something reckless?

104
00:05:33,359 --> 00:05:35,011
Especially since I have a gun?

105
00:05:35,011 --> 00:05:37,939
Jeez, even your jokes are messed up.

106
00:05:37,939 --> 00:05:40,231
- Why do you have a gun...
- If you know I'm joking,

107
00:05:40,231 --> 00:05:42,871
stop worrying and go home.

108
00:05:42,871 --> 00:05:44,651
Didn't you say
your wife's working late tonight?

109
00:05:44,651 --> 00:05:46,351
I'm hanging up.

110
00:06:07,726 --> 00:06:08,923
[My Santa]

111
00:06:08,923 --> 00:06:10,587
I'm working late.

112
00:06:10,587 --> 00:06:12,119
Where are you, Tae Seong?

113
00:06:12,119 --> 00:06:13,592
I'm leaving work now.

114
00:06:13,592 --> 00:06:17,255
Se Ah said she'd watch Yul until eight.
I'll make sure I get home before then.

115
00:06:17,255 --> 00:06:19,423
I won't be too late either.

116
00:06:19,423 --> 00:06:20,626
I'll call you when I'm done.

117
00:06:20,626 --> 00:06:23,383
[Wednesday, May 6]

118
00:06:23,383 --> 00:06:25,891
Jang Eun Hak is leaving work.

119
00:06:25,891 --> 00:06:28,275
He's expected to arrive in
about five minutes.

120
00:06:28,275 --> 00:06:29,975
Okay.

121
00:06:35,992 --> 00:06:38,259
He's entering the next block.

122
00:06:48,311 --> 00:06:51,826
Looks like he's buying something.
He just went into a convenience store.

123
00:06:52,971 --> 00:06:54,659
Oh...

124
00:06:54,659 --> 00:06:56,543
It's liquor.

125
00:06:56,543 --> 00:07:00,999
He grabbed a few bottles of soju
and sat down outside the store.

126
00:07:00,999 --> 00:07:02,926
This could take a while.

127
00:07:11,711 --> 00:07:16,327
Ms. Yoo, there's a man tailing Jang Eun Hak.

128
00:07:16,327 --> 00:07:18,018
- A man?
- Looks like he's been following him

129
00:07:18,018 --> 00:07:19,140
since the workshop.

130
00:07:19,140 --> 00:07:21,811
He's watching him from a distance.

131
00:07:21,811 --> 00:07:23,351
What does he look like?

132
00:07:23,351 --> 00:07:26,339
Wearing a jacket, mid-thirties, maybe?

133
00:07:26,339 --> 00:07:29,871
I can't make out his face on camera.

134
00:07:29,871 --> 00:07:31,592
Let me take a look.

135
00:07:54,575 --> 00:07:57,471
Could it be the son who's a cop...

136
00:07:57,471 --> 00:07:59,079
Yeah, that's him.

137
00:07:59,079 --> 00:08:00,892
Then I guess today...

138
00:08:02,131 --> 00:08:04,059
Let's just watch for now.

139
00:08:17,859 --> 00:08:19,759
Jang Eun Hak is moving.

140
00:08:20,679 --> 00:08:23,335
He's heading back the way he came?

141
00:08:23,335 --> 00:08:25,035
I see him.

142
00:08:42,895 --> 00:08:45,292
Jang Eun Hak has gone back into the workshop.

143
00:08:53,099 --> 00:08:56,495
Ms. Yoo, Jang Eun Hak made a move again.

144
00:08:56,495 --> 00:08:59,026
What? What about the son?

145
00:09:00,187 --> 00:09:01,887
What? Is he hurt?

146
00:09:03,819 --> 00:09:06,155
Jang Eun Hak bolted out.

147
00:09:06,155 --> 00:09:08,759
The son chased right after him.

148
00:09:08,759 --> 00:09:10,892
[Dongwoon Furniture]
He's holding a gun.

149
00:09:28,599 --> 00:09:29,675
I'm heading out.

150
00:09:29,675 --> 00:09:31,559
Track their route and keep me posted.

151
00:09:31,559 --> 00:09:35,519
Ms. Yoo, Kwon Tae Seong is here.

152
00:09:35,519 --> 00:09:36,923
- What?
- He went into the workshop,

153
00:09:36,923 --> 00:09:40,626
came back out, and ran off
in the direction the two of them went.

154
00:09:40,626 --> 00:09:42,511
Why is your husband here...

155
00:09:42,511 --> 00:09:45,295
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo, are you listening?

156
00:09:45,295 --> 00:09:46,687
Yeah, I'm listening.

157
00:09:46,687 --> 00:09:48,635
- Then let's pull out for today...
- No.

158
00:09:48,635 --> 00:09:49,995
If we leave now, we'll lose him.

159
00:09:49,995 --> 00:09:51,695
Keep going.

160
00:09:55,031 --> 00:09:56,531
I'm down. Which way?

161
00:09:56,531 --> 00:09:58,326
Ms. Yoo, what are you going to do?

162
00:09:58,326 --> 00:09:59,719
What if something happens today...

163
00:09:59,719 --> 00:10:01,419
Ki Yeong Do.

164
00:10:06,026 --> 00:10:07,826
With your back to the workshop,
you are on the left.

165
00:10:07,826 --> 00:10:10,799
It's to your right, Ms. Yoo.

166
00:10:10,799 --> 00:10:13,126
Don't take any unnecessary risks.

167
00:11:05,167 --> 00:11:07,192
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

168
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:28,859
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

169
00:11:46,031 --> 00:11:47,731
Meeting concluded.

170
00:11:49,471 --> 00:11:51,819
Good work, Ms. Yoo.

171
00:11:51,819 --> 00:11:54,503
You should get out of there for now.

172
00:11:54,503 --> 00:11:56,203
Dong Jin!

173
00:12:05,735 --> 00:12:06,792
What's wrong with you?

174
00:12:06,792 --> 00:12:08,492
Are you okay?

175
00:12:09,695 --> 00:12:11,395
No...

176
00:12:12,115 --> 00:12:14,195
Not me. I didn't shoot him.

177
00:12:14,195 --> 00:12:18,295
- I know, I know.
- Not me... I...

178
00:12:22,531 --> 00:12:24,231
Kingfisher...

179
00:12:26,735 --> 00:12:28,643
Kingfisher was here.

180
00:12:28,643 --> 00:12:30,207
Kingfisher was here... Kingfisher...

181
00:12:30,207 --> 00:12:32,135
Kingfisher... Kingfisher...

182
00:12:32,135 --> 00:12:34,119
Kingfisher...

183
00:12:34,119 --> 00:12:36,826
Dong Jin!

184
00:12:37,592 --> 00:12:38,592
Dong Jin!

185
00:12:38,592 --> 00:12:40,326
No.

186
00:12:40,959 --> 00:12:42,326
You need to get to a hospital first.

187
00:12:42,326 --> 00:12:44,026
You're hurt right now.

188
00:12:44,026 --> 00:12:45,759
I have to catch him.
I have to catch Kingfisher.

189
00:12:45,759 --> 00:12:48,467
You're bleeding badly now!

190
00:12:48,467 --> 00:12:49,675
He was here.

191
00:12:49,675 --> 00:12:52,192
Kingfisher was right here moments ago.

192
00:12:52,192 --> 00:12:54,992
Lee Dong Jin, Lee Dong Jin.

193
00:12:55,615 --> 00:12:56,943
Pull yourself together.

194
00:12:56,943 --> 00:12:58,692
You have to stay conscious.

195
00:13:00,827 --> 00:13:02,527
Tae Seong.

196
00:13:05,651 --> 00:13:07,792
That punk, Jang Eun Hak...

197
00:13:10,947 --> 00:13:12,647
is dead.

198
00:13:13,683 --> 00:13:15,459
That punk...

199
00:13:19,303 --> 00:13:20,959
He is dead, that punk...

200
00:13:20,959 --> 00:13:25,126
Tae Seong, what do I do? I'm...

201
00:13:27,787 --> 00:13:30,126
I'm so glad that...

202
00:13:33,355 --> 00:13:35,226
Jang Eun Hak is dead.

203
00:13:35,931 --> 00:13:37,631
And...

204
00:13:39,227 --> 00:13:41,595
I'm ashamed of myself for feeling that way.

205
00:13:41,595 --> 00:13:42,947
Dong Jin, it's alright.

206
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:46,192
Dong Jin, it's alright. It's alright.

207
00:13:49,543 --> 00:13:53,259
I was the person in the world
who wanted Jang Eun Hak dead the most.

208
00:13:54,539 --> 00:14:00,183
Every single day, without fail,
I wanted to kill him.

209
00:14:00,183 --> 00:14:03,626
Even after twenty years,
whenever I think about that day...

210
00:14:12,527 --> 00:14:15,992
I imagined shooting him over and over again.

211
00:14:16,691 --> 00:14:21,092
I imagined a hole blown through his head,
his entire body torn to shreds,

212
00:14:22,563 --> 00:14:26,618
writhing in agony, then falling into hell.

213
00:14:26,618 --> 00:14:29,193
I wanted desperately to see it
with my own eyes.

214
00:14:29,193 --> 00:14:31,083
I know. I know, Dong Jin.

215
00:14:31,083 --> 00:14:34,175
But first, let's go to the hospital. Please.

216
00:14:34,175 --> 00:14:36,226
Dong Jin, Dong Jin.

217
00:14:36,226 --> 00:14:38,199
You need to go to the hospital first.

218
00:14:38,199 --> 00:14:40,226
I have to catch Kingfisher.

219
00:14:41,223 --> 00:14:43,695
He killed that punk!

220
00:14:43,695 --> 00:14:46,092
Kingfisher killed that punk.

221
00:14:46,092 --> 00:14:48,624
For twenty years you pictured it
over and over, but couldn't do it.

222
00:14:48,624 --> 00:14:50,659
Kingfisher did.

223
00:14:50,659 --> 00:14:52,126
You saw it, right?

224
00:14:52,126 --> 00:14:55,799
That punk was trying to kill someone again.

225
00:14:55,799 --> 00:14:58,599
That's right. I couldn't do it.

226
00:14:58,599 --> 00:15:01,091
Even when Jang Eun Hak
was running right in front of me,

227
00:15:01,091 --> 00:15:04,426
with the back of his head
right there in front of me,

228
00:15:05,392 --> 00:15:07,159
I still couldn't kill him.

229
00:15:07,159 --> 00:15:08,892
Do you know why?

230
00:15:11,135 --> 00:15:12,207
You asked me before.

231
00:15:12,207 --> 00:15:14,619
What if he didn't change?

232
00:15:14,619 --> 00:15:16,747
But I already had my answer.

233
00:15:16,747 --> 00:15:19,675
If he commits a crime,
I'll catch him and throw him in.

234
00:15:19,675 --> 00:15:22,039
If he gets out and commits another crime,
I'll catch him and throw him in again.

235
00:15:22,039 --> 00:15:23,459
I'll keep catching him and locking him up.

236
00:15:23,459 --> 00:15:26,075
That's my way,
and it's the right thing to do.

237
00:15:26,075 --> 00:15:30,607
No, in reality, those punks never get judged.

238
00:15:30,607 --> 00:15:35,092
Dong Jin, the law isn't perfect.
And you know that, right?

239
00:15:35,092 --> 00:15:36,592
Oh, yeah?

240
00:15:36,592 --> 00:15:38,792
Then do whatever you want.

241
00:15:38,792 --> 00:15:41,331
I don't care whether the law
is perfect or not.

242
00:15:41,331 --> 00:15:43,671
To me, they're just the same punks
who killed people.

243
00:15:43,671 --> 00:15:46,059
And catching punks like that is my job.

244
00:15:48,123 --> 00:15:51,139
I'll do my job, so you do yours.

245
00:15:51,139 --> 00:15:53,759
Write a story, cover a case, whatever.

246
00:15:53,759 --> 00:15:55,592
You're a reporter, right?

247
00:16:03,123 --> 00:16:05,526
Beom, where are you?

248
00:16:17,627 --> 00:16:18,819
Beom.

249
00:16:18,819 --> 00:16:21,763
Comb through all the nearby CCTV footage
and track his escape route.

250
00:16:21,763 --> 00:16:25,559
And collect every fingerprint, footprint,
and trace evidence around the rooftop.

251
00:16:25,559 --> 00:16:27,359
Okay.

252
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:43,803
Se Ah.

253
00:16:43,803 --> 00:16:45,831
- Huh? Oh.
- Sorry for waking you.

254
00:16:45,831 --> 00:16:47,195
Bo Na, you're home?

255
00:16:47,195 --> 00:16:50,611
Well, Tae Seong called earlier
saying he'd be late,

256
00:16:50,611 --> 00:16:52,992
so I washed Yul and put her to bed
in the master bedroom.

257
00:16:52,992 --> 00:16:55,068
Sorry I'm late. Thank you.

258
00:16:55,068 --> 00:16:56,859
Go ahead and do what you need to do.

259
00:17:03,943 --> 00:17:04,954
[My Santa]
Something came up.

260
00:17:04,954 --> 00:17:08,859
I'll be really late tonight.
Don't wait up. Go to bed first.

261
00:17:31,792 --> 00:17:33,955
[Did Kingfisher...]

262
00:17:33,955 --> 00:17:35,726
Did Kingfisher...

263
00:17:36,783 --> 00:17:38,559
see me too?

264
00:17:52,127 --> 00:17:54,659
That man that day...

265
00:17:55,519 --> 00:17:58,139
Was he really Kingfisher?

266
00:17:58,139 --> 00:18:00,692
Goodnight, Tae Seong.

267
00:18:06,195 --> 00:18:08,103
Tae Seong.

268
00:18:08,103 --> 00:18:11,891
I'll do my job, so you do yours.

269
00:18:11,891 --> 00:18:13,692
You're a reporter, right?

270
00:18:15,326 --> 00:18:16,496
[Did Kingfisher see me too?]

271
00:18:16,496 --> 00:18:18,459
[That man that day...
Was he really Kingfisher?]

272
00:18:23,835 --> 00:18:26,827
Exclusive: Kingfisher Crime Scene.

273
00:18:26,827 --> 00:18:28,959
A supermarket murder convict died

274
00:18:28,959 --> 00:18:32,439
after being shot while fleeing
an attempted murder.

275
00:18:32,439 --> 00:18:35,434
Jang Eun Hak, previously imprisoned
for the murder of a supermarket couple

276
00:18:35,434 --> 00:18:37,519
in Gangmyeon-dong 20 years ago,

277
00:18:37,519 --> 00:18:41,959
died after attempting another murder
just one month after his release on parole.

278
00:18:43,919 --> 00:18:45,416
[Unusual Alleyway Attack]
Another Kingfisher incident

279
00:18:45,416 --> 00:18:47,223
[Kingfisher Strikes Again Last Night]
occurred last night.

280
00:18:47,223 --> 00:18:48,890
The victim this time was Mr. Jang,

281
00:18:48,890 --> 00:18:52,087
who had brutally murdered
a supermarket-owning couple 20 years ago.

282
00:18:52,087 --> 00:18:54,148
[Supermarket Murder Convict Shot Dead]
He was sentenced to 16 years,

283
00:18:54,148 --> 00:18:56,264
[While Fleeing After Attempted Murder]
and died a month after being paroled,

284
00:18:56,264 --> 00:18:57,655
[Supermarket Couple Murder Found Dead]
a year before his full term,

285
00:18:57,655 --> 00:18:59,055
[One Month After Parole]
sending shock through the community.

286
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,055
- Moreover, this incident differs from
- They say Kingfisher

287
00:19:00,055 --> 00:19:01,055
- the previous ones,
- struck again yesterday.

288
00:19:01,055 --> 00:19:02,055
- which mainly occurred
- Really?

289
00:19:02,055 --> 00:19:03,055
- in enclosed, isolated spaces.
- Kingfisher is awesome.

290
00:19:03,055 --> 00:19:05,239
Unlike other Kingfisher cases,

291
00:19:05,239 --> 00:19:08,692
this one occurred in a residential alley,
making it highly unusual.

292
00:19:08,692 --> 00:19:11,626
[Exclusive: Kingfisher Crime Scene]
Shockingly, Mr. Jang was revealed

293
00:19:11,626 --> 00:19:13,992
to have attempted to murder his employer.

294
00:19:13,992 --> 00:19:17,436
Just one month after being paroled,
he had committed another attempted murder,

295
00:19:17,436 --> 00:19:18,839
this time as a flagrant offender.

296
00:19:18,839 --> 00:19:21,947
Furthermore, given the urgent situation
with the suspect on the run,

297
00:19:21,947 --> 00:19:23,959
it is speculated that Kingfisher
may have broken from his usual pattern

298
00:19:23,959 --> 00:19:28,226
and carried out the shooting
in a public place.

299
00:19:29,327 --> 00:19:31,195
Mommy, where is Daddy?

300
00:19:31,195 --> 00:19:33,243
Why isn't Daddy waking up?

301
00:19:33,243 --> 00:19:36,583
Dad? Let Daddy sleep a little longer.

302
00:19:36,583 --> 00:19:38,892
Is Daddy a sleepyhead?

303
00:19:40,503 --> 00:19:43,259
Daddy worked late last night, so he's tired.

304
00:19:43,259 --> 00:19:44,891
What work?

305
00:19:44,891 --> 00:19:47,351
Writing articles?

306
00:19:47,351 --> 00:19:49,647
What is an article?

307
00:19:49,647 --> 00:19:53,287
An article is something
that tells people in the world

308
00:19:53,287 --> 00:19:59,027
what happened, why it happened,
and what to do now. That's what it does.

309
00:19:59,027 --> 00:20:00,691
Yul, you finished all of this, right?

310
00:20:00,691 --> 00:20:04,379
Oh? You did? Then let's have this.

311
00:20:04,379 --> 00:20:06,763
You said you want to be tall
like Mommy and Daddy, right?

312
00:20:06,763 --> 00:20:08,792
Then you need to eat this
and grow big and tall.

313
00:20:08,792 --> 00:20:10,659
Here, eat.

314
00:20:11,771 --> 00:20:13,271
Is it good?

315
00:20:13,271 --> 00:20:14,319
It is good!

316
00:20:14,319 --> 00:20:16,019
Yeah?

317
00:20:18,067 --> 00:20:19,259
Daddy!

318
00:20:19,259 --> 00:20:21,483
My little precious! Oh, my!

319
00:20:21,483 --> 00:20:23,703
My treasure!

320
00:20:23,703 --> 00:20:25,511
Did you sleep well?

321
00:20:25,511 --> 00:20:26,826
You're already all dressed?

322
00:20:26,826 --> 00:20:30,526
Yeah. I'm dressed, and I ate this too.

323
00:20:30,526 --> 00:20:33,247
I'm going to be this tall, just like you.

324
00:20:33,247 --> 00:20:35,091
Wow, really? Good job.

325
00:20:35,091 --> 00:20:36,175
Sorry, I overslept.

326
00:20:36,175 --> 00:20:39,999
I will make it up to you tomorrow, okay?

327
00:20:39,999 --> 00:20:42,307
Oh, my.

328
00:20:42,307 --> 00:20:44,411
Why don't you sleep a little longer?
You're already up?

329
00:20:44,411 --> 00:20:46,359
I have to get to work.

330
00:20:50,771 --> 00:20:52,971
You must have been tired
from working late last night too,

331
00:20:52,971 --> 00:20:55,192
and you were probably super busy
all alone today.

332
00:21:00,771 --> 00:21:04,979
What? What's with that meaningful look
so early in the morning...

333
00:21:04,979 --> 00:21:05,979
No, it's not that.

334
00:21:05,979 --> 00:21:08,459
It's the look of someone gazing
at someone precious.

335
00:21:11,323 --> 00:21:14,599
Go wash up. I'll make you some toast.

336
00:21:14,599 --> 00:21:16,415
Just a second.

337
00:21:16,415 --> 00:21:18,759
Let me recharge first.

338
00:21:19,783 --> 00:21:21,483
Me too.

339
00:21:25,435 --> 00:21:27,159
Go wash up.

340
00:21:28,171 --> 00:21:30,659
I'm having two pieces of toast.

341
00:21:32,659 --> 00:21:35,426
[Resignation Letter]

342
00:21:36,827 --> 00:21:38,567
Are you threatening me now?

343
00:21:38,567 --> 00:21:41,239
Say it to my face.
Don't do this with a piece of paper.

344
00:21:41,239 --> 00:21:42,765
I know there's
a Kingfisher countermeasure meeting today,

345
00:21:42,765 --> 00:21:44,939
chaired by the Commissioner General.

346
00:21:44,939 --> 00:21:46,163
So what?

347
00:21:46,163 --> 00:21:47,563
How many times have chiefs had meetings?

348
00:21:47,563 --> 00:21:49,015
Don't you know
those meetings are just for show?

349
00:21:49,015 --> 00:21:50,723
Then please make sure
this one isn't just for show.

350
00:21:50,723 --> 00:21:52,239
How exactly am I supposed to do that?

351
00:21:52,239 --> 00:21:54,599
What, you want me to put you in charge?

352
00:21:54,599 --> 00:21:55,663
Why would I?

353
00:21:55,663 --> 00:21:57,492
This is my case.

354
00:21:58,219 --> 00:22:01,255
What were you doing yesterday,
and now you come here?

355
00:22:01,255 --> 00:22:04,163
You finally came face-to-face
with the man you wanted to catch so badly.

356
00:22:04,163 --> 00:22:06,092
But why didn't you catch him?

357
00:22:06,995 --> 00:22:08,695
Jeez.

358
00:22:09,575 --> 00:22:12,563
Other stations asked me
whether you deliberately let him get away.

359
00:22:12,563 --> 00:22:15,891
They think you were stalling to give the guy

360
00:22:15,891 --> 00:22:18,326
who took your revenge for you time to escape.

361
00:22:19,827 --> 00:22:21,923
If that's the case,

362
00:22:21,923 --> 00:22:24,603
it'll be grounds for an investigation
and disciplinary action.

363
00:22:24,603 --> 00:22:30,853
Including why you were lurking around
Jang Eun Hak at that time.

364
00:22:31,695 --> 00:22:34,292
You don't think this will come up
in today's meeting?

365
00:22:38,287 --> 00:22:41,711
Only you know the truth.

366
00:22:41,711 --> 00:22:42,951
I won't ask you about it.

367
00:22:42,951 --> 00:22:44,826
But you need to let it go too.

368
00:22:45,847 --> 00:22:50,923
If an investigation or disciplinary action
comes up, I'll cover for you.

369
00:22:50,923 --> 00:22:52,623
You can go now.

370
00:22:53,971 --> 00:22:56,643
I won't make excuses.
I'll take responsibility.

371
00:22:56,643 --> 00:22:58,595
If they tell me to accept
the punishment, I will.

372
00:22:58,595 --> 00:23:00,379
If they give me a chance, I'll make it right.

373
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:02,392
And if neither is possible...

374
00:23:02,392 --> 00:23:04,355
[Resignation Letter]

375
00:23:04,355 --> 00:23:06,571
Please accept my resignation.

376
00:23:06,571 --> 00:23:08,347
Hey, take this back.

377
00:23:08,347 --> 00:23:09,807
Hey, Lee Dong Jin.

378
00:23:09,807 --> 00:23:11,559
Hey, Dong Jin.

379
00:23:12,355 --> 00:23:15,792
Jeez, he's bowing, which he never does.

380
00:23:21,731 --> 00:23:23,815
Oh, Mr. Lee.

381
00:23:23,815 --> 00:23:26,451
As expected, all the CCTV footage
around the area was wiped.

382
00:23:26,451 --> 00:23:29,091
It was a no-parking zone, so there wasn't
anything useful from dashcams either.

383
00:23:29,091 --> 00:23:31,623
There's a public parking lot in the back.

384
00:23:31,623 --> 00:23:32,623
I saw it.

385
00:23:32,623 --> 00:23:33,795
You did?

386
00:23:33,795 --> 00:23:36,619
Most of the people living there
work in the furniture district,

387
00:23:36,619 --> 00:23:39,559
so it's normally deserted at that hour
because everyone goes to bed early.

388
00:23:39,559 --> 00:23:42,492
Jeez, and no word on any witnesses, either.

389
00:23:43,343 --> 00:23:44,695
What about forensics?

390
00:23:44,695 --> 00:23:47,675
Nothing yet. Doesn't look like
they recovered much from the scene.

391
00:23:47,675 --> 00:23:50,343
But you never know what might turn up,
so keep checking regularly.

392
00:23:50,343 --> 00:23:51,875
Okay.

393
00:23:51,875 --> 00:23:53,783
But are you okay, Mr. Lee?

394
00:23:53,783 --> 00:23:56,515
How do you think I feel after letting him
slip away right in front of me?

395
00:23:56,515 --> 00:23:57,919
No, I didn't mean that.

396
00:23:57,919 --> 00:24:00,859
The victim, Jang Eun Hak, is that person...

397
00:24:02,419 --> 00:24:04,487
Enough.

398
00:24:04,487 --> 00:24:07,715
What happened with those couple of
assault suspects from last time?

399
00:24:07,715 --> 00:24:09,691
Nothing yet on that one.

400
00:24:09,691 --> 00:24:11,926
The cybercrime unit
hasn't found anything either.

401
00:24:13,355 --> 00:24:16,099
So what are you going to do without me?

402
00:24:16,099 --> 00:24:18,519
What? Why would you be gone?

403
00:24:18,519 --> 00:24:20,219
Where are you going?

404
00:24:21,859 --> 00:24:23,535
[Civil Servant ID, Lee Dong Jin]

405
00:24:23,535 --> 00:24:25,127
You're getting a new mentor soon.

406
00:24:25,127 --> 00:24:29,492
Keep your eyes open
and learn everything you can.

407
00:24:30,931 --> 00:24:33,392
And don't make your previous mentor look bad.

408
00:24:37,399 --> 00:24:40,087
Wait, you're not quitting, are you?
You're not, right?

409
00:24:40,087 --> 00:24:42,043
Jeez, where are you going?

410
00:24:42,043 --> 00:24:43,887
I'm going to sleep.

411
00:24:43,887 --> 00:24:45,426
Now of all times?

412
00:24:45,426 --> 00:24:47,592
[Investigative Reporting Team]

413
00:24:47,592 --> 00:24:48,692
[Kwon Tae Seong]

414
00:24:48,692 --> 00:24:50,359
[Kingfisher, Search Results]

415
00:24:50,359 --> 00:24:52,092
[Kingfisher: Notorious Killer
or Avenger of Justice?]

416
00:24:53,192 --> 00:24:54,192
An avenger of justice...

417
00:24:54,192 --> 00:24:55,973
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong
tracked the cases involving Kingfisher]

418
00:24:55,973 --> 00:24:57,259
[and found what they had in common]

419
00:24:58,726 --> 00:25:00,392
[Five Reflections on Kingfisher]

420
00:25:00,392 --> 00:25:03,926
[The Painful Questions Kingfisher
Forces Our Society to Ask]

421
00:25:04,792 --> 00:25:07,126
[Even if Kingfisher is caught tomorrow,
the questions he raised will remain]

422
00:25:07,126 --> 00:25:08,826
[Kwon Tae Seong, Social Affairs Reporter]

423
00:25:09,526 --> 00:25:11,811
Wow! As expected of Kwon Tae Seong.

424
00:25:11,811 --> 00:25:15,335
His comeback piece on Kingfisher
is an on-the-ground exclusive too.

425
00:25:15,335 --> 00:25:17,715
Ms. Gu, did you go there with him?

426
00:25:17,715 --> 00:25:20,807
Oh, no, I didn't know about it.

427
00:25:20,807 --> 00:25:23,931
Really? What? He acted like
he wasn't interested,

428
00:25:23,931 --> 00:25:26,303
but he was digging into it on his own?

429
00:25:26,303 --> 00:25:28,219
So it was all an act.

430
00:25:28,219 --> 00:25:29,287
But why isn't he here?

431
00:25:29,287 --> 00:25:31,459
We need a follow-up article fast.

432
00:25:34,759 --> 00:25:37,479
Let's focus on the parole system
for our next piece.

433
00:25:37,479 --> 00:25:41,551
Let's look into possible loopholes
in Jang Eun Hak's parole review process,

434
00:25:41,551 --> 00:25:44,995
and focus on preventive measures
so this kind of thing doesn't happen again.

435
00:25:44,995 --> 00:25:47,747
Based on your research,
prepare a draft article.

436
00:25:47,747 --> 00:25:48,992
I have somewhere else I need to go today.

437
00:25:48,992 --> 00:25:50,123
What's he saying? Why isn't he coming?

438
00:25:50,123 --> 00:25:52,943
Oh, I don't know about that.

439
00:25:52,943 --> 00:25:54,883
He just told me to prepare the article.

440
00:25:54,883 --> 00:25:58,219
Oh! A quick follow-up story? I like it.

441
00:25:58,219 --> 00:25:59,919
What's the angle?

442
00:26:01,767 --> 00:26:05,591
The homework Kingfisher left us?

443
00:26:05,591 --> 00:26:08,447
Oh, homework?

444
00:26:08,447 --> 00:26:10,147
What's that supposed to mean?

445
00:26:17,447 --> 00:26:19,147
Director Yoo

446
00:26:19,759 --> 00:26:23,487
must have been quite surprised
by her husband's article.

447
00:26:23,487 --> 00:26:25,259
She knew about it.

448
00:26:26,183 --> 00:26:29,891
- What?
- She fired, knowing her husband was coming.

449
00:26:29,891 --> 00:26:35,767
She probably figured that if she missed
the shot, more people might get hurt.

450
00:26:35,767 --> 00:26:39,607
What if she bumped into her husband?

451
00:26:39,607 --> 00:26:41,959
She probably factored all of that
into her decision.

452
00:26:42,859 --> 00:26:45,626
Because she has never once been wrong.

453
00:26:46,631 --> 00:26:50,219
She's never been wrong. Never made a mistake.

454
00:26:50,219 --> 00:26:53,991
Anyway, Assistant Manager Ki,
you must've had a hard time.

455
00:26:53,991 --> 00:26:58,855
I erased what I could
and checked for witnesses and vehicles,

456
00:26:58,855 --> 00:27:03,267
but the area was huge,
so I'm not sure we covered every route.

457
00:27:03,267 --> 00:27:06,519
We didn't get a chance to check
the new sniper position afterward, either.

458
00:27:06,519 --> 00:27:09,111
Getting out quickly was our priority.

459
00:27:09,111 --> 00:27:11,463
So now,

460
00:27:11,463 --> 00:27:14,503
we don't know where something
could come from, huh?

461
00:27:14,503 --> 00:27:18,419
So far, nothing concerning
has appeared in the police database.

462
00:27:18,419 --> 00:27:20,959
Keep monitoring it closely.

463
00:27:21,703 --> 00:27:25,479
And for the time being,
let's leave out the sniper stuff.

464
00:27:25,479 --> 00:27:27,239
Understood.

465
00:27:27,239 --> 00:27:28,939
Good work.

466
00:27:35,139 --> 00:27:37,391
Let's give you a bath, Tae Soon.

467
00:27:37,391 --> 00:27:41,115
You'll start to smell
if you don't get washed regularly.

468
00:27:41,115 --> 00:27:46,035
Yoo Bo Na must have had a great time,
like flying high, right?

469
00:27:46,035 --> 00:27:47,926
Shall we wash your hair too?

470
00:27:52,399 --> 00:27:56,615
Ah, you're so pretty.

471
00:27:56,615 --> 00:27:59,792
Nice and cool.

472
00:28:18,767 --> 00:28:20,559
Wow, look at all this dust.

473
00:28:22,243 --> 00:28:25,787
How can this be where our Director Yoo stays,
even for a minute?

474
00:28:25,787 --> 00:28:28,883
Jeez, move over there a bit!

475
00:28:28,883 --> 00:28:31,471
I'm going to get lung inflammation
from this, seriously.

476
00:28:31,471 --> 00:28:36,159
I can't sleep at night. I can't sleep.

477
00:28:37,931 --> 00:28:41,307
Our great Kingfisher
should be resting well today.

478
00:28:41,307 --> 00:28:44,231
But what is she doing?
Is she sleeping soundly?

479
00:28:44,231 --> 00:28:48,127
Even the way she sleeps must be totally cool.

480
00:28:48,127 --> 00:28:50,023
Oh, seriously, what are these?

481
00:28:50,023 --> 00:28:52,995
Keep this stuff cleaned up!

482
00:28:52,995 --> 00:28:54,992
Jeez.

483
00:28:54,992 --> 00:28:56,871
Ugh. What got on it, seriously?

484
00:28:56,871 --> 00:28:59,492
This is expensive,
and it can't even be dry-cleaned.

485
00:29:00,635 --> 00:29:03,127
How long has that trash been sitting here?

486
00:29:03,127 --> 00:29:05,959
Tae Soon, you got scared, didn't you?

487
00:29:07,692 --> 00:29:09,779
Are you really not going to help?

488
00:29:09,779 --> 00:29:11,479
Clean this up, now!

489
00:29:25,303 --> 00:29:27,631
Training's pretty intense today?

490
00:29:27,631 --> 00:29:30,359
You usually train like this
when you have a lot on your mind.

491
00:29:33,807 --> 00:29:36,623
I felt like my body was a bit stiff.

492
00:29:36,623 --> 00:29:40,192
Yesterday's mission was intense too.
You should get some rest.

493
00:29:44,351 --> 00:29:45,915
What about the shop?

494
00:29:45,915 --> 00:29:47,471
What if a customer comes?

495
00:29:47,471 --> 00:29:50,487
The only customers I have are flies.

496
00:29:50,487 --> 00:29:52,992
Guess I'll help you make a few more sales.

497
00:29:55,239 --> 00:29:58,259
Looks like your husband was at the scene.

498
00:29:59,823 --> 00:30:01,735
It's nothing you need to worry about.

499
00:30:01,735 --> 00:30:04,326
If it's work,
there's no reason for me to worry.

500
00:30:13,135 --> 00:30:15,571
Yul must have grown a lot lately.

501
00:30:15,571 --> 00:30:19,526
She's asking what her daddy does.

502
00:30:21,159 --> 00:30:26,659
I tell her, "Well, your daddy is someone
who does this kind of work."

503
00:30:29,192 --> 00:30:31,392
She may not understand now,

504
00:30:32,011 --> 00:30:34,291
but someday she will, right?

505
00:30:34,291 --> 00:30:36,771
What kind of person her daddy is.

506
00:30:36,771 --> 00:30:39,092
She'll be proud of him.

507
00:30:40,451 --> 00:30:43,792
That's the kind of work he does.

508
00:30:44,611 --> 00:30:47,226
It's when he's doing that work
that he really shines.

509
00:30:50,199 --> 00:30:55,626
He does his job, and I do mine.

510
00:30:57,375 --> 00:31:00,015
As for the unavoidable variables
that come up along the way...

511
00:31:00,015 --> 00:31:05,659
well, I'll manage them
just like I did in the field.

512
00:31:06,931 --> 00:31:09,411
Isn't that what you taught me?

513
00:31:09,411 --> 00:31:10,767
I did?

514
00:31:10,767 --> 00:31:15,426
Well, that was so long ago.
I barely remember.

515
00:31:21,235 --> 00:31:22,683
[Hye Ri's Mom]
This is Hye Ri's mom.

516
00:31:22,683 --> 00:31:24,827
You got the call from the daycare, right?

517
00:31:24,827 --> 00:31:27,911
Don't you think we need to talk?

518
00:31:27,911 --> 00:31:31,359
Why? What's the problem this time?

519
00:31:31,359 --> 00:31:35,339
[Yul's Daycare]

520
00:31:35,339 --> 00:31:37,792
Yes, Miss.

521
00:31:37,792 --> 00:31:39,492
Yul?

522
00:31:42,015 --> 00:31:43,959
Oh...

523
00:31:43,959 --> 00:31:45,692
Really?

524
00:32:04,459 --> 00:32:08,075
Assistant Manager Ki, this is Kwon Se Ah.

525
00:32:08,075 --> 00:32:10,783
I got your number from Bo Na
and wanted to reach out.

526
00:32:10,783 --> 00:32:13,923
I'd like to return your cleaned clothes.

527
00:32:13,923 --> 00:32:17,759
When would be convenient?

528
00:32:20,875 --> 00:32:22,692
Just throw them...

529
00:32:36,783 --> 00:32:38,792
Let's meet after work today.

530
00:32:40,751 --> 00:32:42,631
Today!

531
00:32:42,631 --> 00:32:44,359
Yeah!

532
00:32:44,359 --> 00:32:47,363
Hey, Kwon Se Ah! You can do this, right?

533
00:32:47,363 --> 00:32:48,526
Today's the day!

534
00:32:48,526 --> 00:32:52,026
He said let's meet today,
not tomorrow. What do I do?

535
00:32:52,795 --> 00:32:53,926
Oh?

536
00:32:53,926 --> 00:32:55,726
Oh, jeez.

537
00:32:57,543 --> 00:32:58,879
[Mr. Tiger]
What are you doing now?

538
00:32:58,879 --> 00:33:01,103
I'm a little down today.
Let's just grab a meal.

539
00:33:01,103 --> 00:33:02,803
What?

540
00:33:07,255 --> 00:33:09,371
The customer's phone is turned off...

541
00:33:09,371 --> 00:33:14,226
Seriously, where is he hiding
with his phone turned off?

542
00:33:14,892 --> 00:33:18,151
Was the shock of missing
Kingfisher too much for him?

543
00:33:18,151 --> 00:33:19,726
He's not really quitting, is he?

544
00:33:19,726 --> 00:33:22,326
[You have a new message]

545
00:33:24,092 --> 00:33:26,292
Eat by yourself. I'm busy.

546
00:33:27,839 --> 00:33:30,915
Another date today?
With your sister-in-law again?

547
00:33:30,915 --> 00:33:32,451
No. Today it's with a guy.

548
00:33:32,451 --> 00:33:33,863
Oh, with a guy.

549
00:33:33,863 --> 00:33:36,547
W-W-With a guy?

550
00:33:36,547 --> 00:33:38,247
With who?

551
00:33:44,059 --> 00:33:47,992
Yul, did something happen at kindergarten?

552
00:33:48,807 --> 00:33:50,507
Look at Mommy.

553
00:33:55,579 --> 00:33:58,807
Can you tell me what happened?

554
00:33:58,807 --> 00:34:01,619
That way, I can help you.

555
00:34:01,619 --> 00:34:05,783
Yul, I'm your best friend, remember?

556
00:34:05,783 --> 00:34:08,959
Best friends don't keep secrets
from each other.

557
00:34:10,111 --> 00:34:13,659
Mommy...

558
00:34:14,383 --> 00:34:16,011
Mommy.

559
00:34:16,011 --> 00:34:17,203
Oh, I see.

560
00:34:17,203 --> 00:34:19,963
Were you upset?

561
00:34:19,963 --> 00:34:22,959
Oh, dear. You were upset? Okay.

562
00:34:22,959 --> 00:34:25,492
I'm sorry. I understand.

563
00:34:28,399 --> 00:34:30,392
Mommy.

564
00:35:09,491 --> 00:35:13,292
A punk who shot a dad dead

565
00:35:14,175 --> 00:35:17,171
right in front of his seven-year-old son.

566
00:35:17,171 --> 00:35:22,467
The kid was so traumatized
that he still can't speak.

567
00:35:22,467 --> 00:35:27,947
A normal human being
wouldn't kill a parent in front of a child.

568
00:35:27,947 --> 00:35:32,359
No matter how vile the criminal was,
that still isn't right, right?

569
00:35:42,819 --> 00:35:45,203
What is it? What do you want?

570
00:35:45,203 --> 00:35:49,287
Does an elderly lady
and her grandson live here?

571
00:35:49,287 --> 00:35:50,992
An elderly lady?

572
00:35:51,687 --> 00:35:55,075
Oh, you must mean the people
who lived here before.

573
00:35:55,075 --> 00:35:57,726
I moved in last year.

574
00:35:59,295 --> 00:36:01,192
Okay, I see.

575
00:36:01,192 --> 00:36:02,911
[Ongsan Dream Real Estate]
Oh, that old lady?

576
00:36:02,911 --> 00:36:05,385
- She went to a nursing home last year.
- A nursing home?

577
00:36:05,385 --> 00:36:08,219
She had dementia or something
starting a few years ago.

578
00:36:08,219 --> 00:36:11,567
She's probably been a bit
in and out of it mentally for a while.

579
00:36:11,567 --> 00:36:15,447
Then what about the kid...
She had a grandson, didn't she?

580
00:36:15,447 --> 00:36:17,047
Her grandson?

581
00:36:17,047 --> 00:36:20,583
Oh, the boy who spoke strangely
and barely talked?

582
00:36:20,583 --> 00:36:25,527
Yeah. He'd been pretty troubled
ever since what happened to his dad.

583
00:36:25,527 --> 00:36:27,859
Do you happen to know where he is now?

584
00:36:27,859 --> 00:36:29,899
Didn't he end up in some kind of institution?

585
00:36:29,899 --> 00:36:31,419
Yeah, that's right.

586
00:36:31,419 --> 00:36:35,592
There was no one to take care of him,
so I think he went to an orphanage.

587
00:36:37,571 --> 00:36:39,315
Here.

588
00:36:39,315 --> 00:36:42,019
Sorry I'm returning these so late,
Assistant Manager Ki.

589
00:36:42,019 --> 00:36:44,526
They've been cleaned for a while,

590
00:36:44,526 --> 00:36:48,279
but I wasn't sure
how to get them back to you.

591
00:36:48,279 --> 00:36:49,979
Okay.

592
00:36:51,115 --> 00:36:52,815
Yeah.

593
00:36:54,671 --> 00:36:55,971
Don't you have anything else to say?

594
00:36:55,971 --> 00:36:57,523
Pardon?

595
00:36:57,523 --> 00:37:01,192
Oh, I guess it's my turn to talk.

596
00:37:02,059 --> 00:37:04,426
I believe we had a date planned.

597
00:37:06,931 --> 00:37:10,043
Oh, you remember.

598
00:37:10,043 --> 00:37:13,507
Then shall we start with dinner?

599
00:37:13,507 --> 00:37:15,207
I'm fine without eating.

600
00:37:21,131 --> 00:37:23,111
Hey, what are you doing here?

601
00:37:23,111 --> 00:37:25,715
You! Why are you here?
How did you know I was here?

602
00:37:25,715 --> 00:37:26,726
You told me.

603
00:37:26,726 --> 00:37:27,726
Huh?

604
00:37:27,726 --> 00:37:30,626
"Hey, where are you?" "Me? Yun Cafe."

605
00:37:30,626 --> 00:37:32,127
I've been looking everywhere for you.

606
00:37:32,127 --> 00:37:34,035
Why?

607
00:37:34,035 --> 00:37:36,991
Hello. I'm Beom Seong Hun,
Se Dol's friend here.

608
00:37:36,991 --> 00:37:38,187
I've heard a lot about you.

609
00:37:38,187 --> 00:37:40,292
Hey, what have I even said about him...

610
00:37:40,292 --> 00:37:41,292
No, I didn't.

611
00:37:41,292 --> 00:37:42,707
If it's not rude, may I join you?

612
00:37:42,707 --> 00:37:46,051
No, it is rude. It's very rude.
You're being incredibly rude.

613
00:37:46,051 --> 00:37:50,011
Oh, he might seem a bit clueless,
but he's definitely not a bad guy.

614
00:37:50,011 --> 00:37:52,995
First of all, his job is a cop.

615
00:37:52,995 --> 00:37:55,492
Can't you see this isn't exactly
the place for you right now?

616
00:37:55,492 --> 00:37:58,719
Why don't you leave while I'm asking nicely?

617
00:37:58,719 --> 00:38:01,095
Hey, why isn't this the place for me?

618
00:38:01,095 --> 00:38:02,735
Don't you know the world is
a dangerous place these days?

619
00:38:02,735 --> 00:38:04,048
Even if he looks innocent on the outside,

620
00:38:04,048 --> 00:38:07,393
an expert like me needs to scan him
and see if he's rotten on the inside.

621
00:38:07,393 --> 00:38:08,926
You, seriously...

622
00:38:09,923 --> 00:38:13,847
Not that I'm saying that's what you are,
of course. Don't get me wrong.

623
00:38:13,847 --> 00:38:17,492
We were just about to
go get something to eat.

624
00:38:18,447 --> 00:38:20,787
Shall we get going?

625
00:38:20,787 --> 00:38:21,979
Oh, food!

626
00:38:21,979 --> 00:38:23,126
Hey, perfect timing.

627
00:38:23,126 --> 00:38:25,415
I was just getting hungry.

628
00:38:25,415 --> 00:38:28,559
Well, since we've met like this,
why don't we have a meal together?

629
00:38:28,559 --> 00:38:29,739
I know a good place nearby.

630
00:38:29,739 --> 00:38:33,455
Assistant Manager Ki, we'll go ahead.
Can you come out in a little while?

631
00:38:33,455 --> 00:38:34,879
Sure.

632
00:38:34,879 --> 00:38:36,592
- Come on out!
- Hey.

633
00:38:39,599 --> 00:38:40,679
Oh, seriously.

634
00:38:40,679 --> 00:38:43,907
Hey, put this down.

635
00:38:43,907 --> 00:38:45,787
Hey, do you have a gun on you right now?

636
00:38:45,787 --> 00:38:47,251
Do you think I would? What's with the gun?

637
00:38:47,251 --> 00:38:49,326
So I can blow your head off!

638
00:38:49,326 --> 00:38:51,226
Hey, that hurts!

639
00:38:51,999 --> 00:38:53,051
I came because I was worried about you, okay?

640
00:38:53,051 --> 00:38:55,159
About what?

641
00:38:55,159 --> 00:38:57,107
You know I've got good instincts, right?

642
00:38:57,107 --> 00:38:59,619
Oh, you do? You do?

643
00:38:59,619 --> 00:39:02,492
There's something off about that guy.

644
00:39:02,492 --> 00:39:04,631
Like he reeks of a brutal crime or something?

645
00:39:04,631 --> 00:39:06,826
He's my sister-in-law's coworker, got it?

646
00:39:08,031 --> 00:39:11,759
Then that whole company sounds suspicious.

647
00:39:11,759 --> 00:39:13,307
Hmm...

648
00:39:13,307 --> 00:39:15,727
If you don't have a gun,
I'll use my bare hands, you punk!

649
00:39:15,727 --> 00:39:17,359
Why did you come here? Aren't you leaving?

650
00:39:17,359 --> 00:39:20,092
Why'd you come here just to piss me off?

651
00:39:20,092 --> 00:39:22,359
- Hey, that's enough.
- Where is it?

652
00:39:23,727 --> 00:39:25,055
That restaurant.

653
00:39:25,055 --> 00:39:26,755
What?

654
00:39:33,559 --> 00:39:37,183
This is the kind of chicken feet place
you can't quit once you've tried it.

655
00:39:37,183 --> 00:39:39,936
Alright, starting with
whole chicken feet, spicy chicken feet,

656
00:39:39,936 --> 00:39:41,335
boneless chicken feet,
and braised chicken feet.

657
00:39:41,335 --> 00:39:43,807
For the record, our usual move
is to start with the soupy ones

658
00:39:43,807 --> 00:39:45,726
and finish with the grilled spicy ones.

659
00:39:45,726 --> 00:39:47,279
Do you like chicken feet?

660
00:39:47,279 --> 00:39:49,626
Sometimes. Very occasionally.

661
00:39:49,626 --> 00:39:52,626
They're also packed with collagen, you know.

662
00:39:56,067 --> 00:39:57,211
Can't you eat them?

663
00:39:57,211 --> 00:40:00,826
No. I'm going to give them
a try starting today.

664
00:40:00,826 --> 00:40:02,626
Then please enjoy.

665
00:40:12,327 --> 00:40:14,027
Cheers!

666
00:40:17,715 --> 00:40:19,415
Cheers!

667
00:40:22,131 --> 00:40:23,267
This is so good.

668
00:40:23,267 --> 00:40:26,392
You said you're a cop. What division?

669
00:40:27,487 --> 00:40:29,492
Criminal Affairs, Violent Crimes.

670
00:40:30,219 --> 00:40:32,491
Oh, Violent Crimes.

671
00:40:32,491 --> 00:40:35,559
You must get some interesting cases.

672
00:40:35,559 --> 00:40:37,207
Plenty of horrible ones.

673
00:40:37,207 --> 00:40:39,399
People die, get hurt, get messed up.

674
00:40:39,399 --> 00:40:42,359
What case have you been working on lately?

675
00:40:44,159 --> 00:40:46,371
That's confidential.

676
00:40:46,371 --> 00:40:50,659
You seem really interested in crime, though?

677
00:40:51,703 --> 00:40:53,907
I'm interested in profiling.

678
00:40:53,907 --> 00:40:56,259
I majored in psychology too.

679
00:40:57,292 --> 00:40:59,711
You majored in psychology.

680
00:40:59,711 --> 00:41:01,426
That's impressive.

681
00:41:02,079 --> 00:41:04,326
Then let me give you a scenario.

682
00:41:04,326 --> 00:41:06,892
Want to try profiling it for fun?

683
00:41:07,979 --> 00:41:10,095
Sounds fun.

684
00:41:10,095 --> 00:41:12,267
Okay, a man

685
00:41:12,267 --> 00:41:15,859
was shot dead through a gap
in a motel window by a sniper rifle.

686
00:41:16,531 --> 00:41:18,383
Who's the killer?

687
00:41:18,383 --> 00:41:20,507
Are you kidding? The whole country knows.

688
00:41:20,507 --> 00:41:21,643
It happened yesterday too.

689
00:41:21,643 --> 00:41:23,551
Hey, do you think I'd ask about that?

690
00:41:23,551 --> 00:41:27,059
Who do you think Kingfisher really is?

691
00:41:28,067 --> 00:41:29,767
I'm not sure.

692
00:41:30,839 --> 00:41:35,192
The police don't have enough evidence
to make an inference like that.

693
00:41:36,126 --> 00:41:41,043
The whole process is extremely methodical,
and he leaves no evidence behind.

694
00:41:41,043 --> 00:41:44,226
That's why I have a theory.

695
00:41:44,226 --> 00:41:48,959
"Maybe Kingfisher isn't acting alone?"
That kind of.

696
00:41:50,739 --> 00:41:52,251
That's possible.

697
00:41:52,251 --> 00:41:54,659
His methods do seem highly organized.

698
00:41:55,887 --> 00:41:59,426
But you sound pretty certain, though?

699
00:42:01,619 --> 00:42:04,226
That he never leaves any evidence.

700
00:42:04,859 --> 00:42:07,192
That's why the police
haven't caught him yet, right?

701
00:42:07,891 --> 00:42:10,379
Ma'am, one more order of
chicken feet in broth, please.

702
00:42:10,379 --> 00:42:12,183
Yeah.

703
00:42:12,183 --> 00:42:13,526
Hey!

704
00:42:13,526 --> 00:42:15,647
Did you really eat all that
by yourself already?

705
00:42:15,647 --> 00:42:17,715
Me?

706
00:42:17,715 --> 00:42:19,415
Oh, my.

707
00:42:25,279 --> 00:42:27,992
Wait, you've got something on you.

708
00:42:38,327 --> 00:42:40,635
Thank you.

709
00:42:40,635 --> 00:42:43,092
It's nice to see someone
with such a good appetite.

710
00:42:46,226 --> 00:42:49,459
I usually eat pretty well.

711
00:42:49,459 --> 00:42:51,826
Assistant Manager Ki,
you should eat some too.

712
00:42:51,826 --> 00:42:54,915
Oh, I'm fine. I don't really eat that much.

713
00:42:54,915 --> 00:42:56,039
Oh, right.

714
00:42:56,039 --> 00:42:58,659
You did say you don't eat much, right?

715
00:42:59,539 --> 00:43:01,315
I should get going.

716
00:43:01,315 --> 00:43:02,492
I need to head back to the station.

717
00:43:02,492 --> 00:43:03,767
Yeah? You sure?

718
00:43:03,767 --> 00:43:05,415
Go ahead, bye.

719
00:43:05,415 --> 00:43:07,255
Don't forget to pay on your way out.

720
00:43:07,255 --> 00:43:09,607
Yeah, just stay and have some fun.

721
00:43:09,607 --> 00:43:12,159
Maybe we'll see each other again sometime.

722
00:43:25,435 --> 00:43:29,059
Wow! Looks like Se Dol
finally escaped the single life.

723
00:43:30,623 --> 00:43:33,826
Jeez, but why do I feel like this?

724
00:43:39,939 --> 00:43:43,092
Wow, one beer here costs...

725
00:43:43,092 --> 00:43:45,126
Is this some fancy place?

726
00:43:45,775 --> 00:43:48,726
Everyone, let's be prepared.

727
00:43:48,726 --> 00:43:52,192
We need to nip this in the bud.

728
00:43:58,847 --> 00:44:01,191
Both of you are here as well.

729
00:44:01,191 --> 00:44:03,492
Thanks for showing up.

730
00:44:05,427 --> 00:44:08,099
This isn't just about Hye Ri.

731
00:44:08,099 --> 00:44:13,047
Who knows whose child could be next?

732
00:44:13,047 --> 00:44:16,326
I ordered some beer and snacks. Is beer okay?

733
00:44:16,326 --> 00:44:19,131
Oh, absolutely. Beer sounds great.

734
00:44:19,131 --> 00:44:23,339
Well, since we're at a bar,
we might as well have a drink.

735
00:44:23,339 --> 00:44:25,403
What are you talking about, beer?

736
00:44:25,403 --> 00:44:28,687
We left the kids at home,
so let's keep this short and wrap it up.

737
00:44:28,687 --> 00:44:33,443
Just because of some stupid blocks,
those two kids ganged up and hurt Hye Ri.

738
00:44:33,443 --> 00:44:36,275
She must've been so upset.

739
00:44:36,275 --> 00:44:39,059
She came home and wouldn't even
eat her favorite pork cutlet...

740
00:44:40,847 --> 00:44:42,383
Oh, my.

741
00:44:42,383 --> 00:44:45,023
What's this?

742
00:44:45,023 --> 00:44:47,826
Is that Yul's finger?

743
00:44:48,735 --> 00:44:51,083
Oh, my God. What happened?

744
00:44:51,083 --> 00:44:53,475
Every time Seo Jun built something
with the blocks,

745
00:44:53,475 --> 00:44:54,991
Hye Ri would come and knock it down.

746
00:44:54,991 --> 00:44:58,426
So Yul tried to stop her.

747
00:44:58,426 --> 00:45:02,659
Then Hye Ri bit Yul's finger.

748
00:45:03,775 --> 00:45:07,795
Seo Jun got scared and pushed Hye Ri away.

749
00:45:07,795 --> 00:45:10,563
As far as he's concerned,
he was only trying to separate them.

750
00:45:10,563 --> 00:45:14,451
Wait, Hye Ri bit Yul?

751
00:45:14,451 --> 00:45:16,079
Hye Ri didn't mention any of that.

752
00:45:16,079 --> 00:45:20,723
Oh, maybe she was afraid you'd scold her,
so she didn't tell you.

753
00:45:20,723 --> 00:45:23,547
Oh, that must've hurt.

754
00:45:23,547 --> 00:45:28,726
Why didn't Yul tell the teacher about this?

755
00:45:30,347 --> 00:45:31,347
Wait.

756
00:45:31,347 --> 00:45:35,011
So did you call us here
to complain about this?

757
00:45:35,011 --> 00:45:37,459
To get an apology out of me?

758
00:45:38,495 --> 00:45:40,726
Hye Ri's mom.

759
00:45:40,726 --> 00:45:42,226
Yeah?

760
00:45:42,226 --> 00:45:45,859
No, why? What is it?

761
00:45:46,863 --> 00:45:52,126
As a mom, what am I supposed
to do in a situation like this...

762
00:45:53,399 --> 00:45:55,555
I honestly don't know.

763
00:45:55,555 --> 00:45:59,326
So I just told Yul what felt right to me.

764
00:45:59,326 --> 00:46:01,320
I told Yul that Hye Ri didn't do it
because she hated Yul.

765
00:46:01,320 --> 00:46:04,026
She was probably just upset for a moment.

766
00:46:09,051 --> 00:46:13,179
Well, the kids still have to
live together going forward.

767
00:46:13,179 --> 00:46:15,675
We need to comfort them
so this doesn't leave a bad memory,

768
00:46:15,675 --> 00:46:20,525
and help them get along better from now on.

769
00:46:20,525 --> 00:46:24,992
I think that's what adults should do.

770
00:46:25,611 --> 00:46:30,935
So I wanted to ask for your advice
on how to do that.

771
00:46:30,935 --> 00:46:32,699
Oh, what is there to do?

772
00:46:32,699 --> 00:46:35,859
Just discipline them
if they did something wrong,

773
00:46:35,859 --> 00:46:40,955
have them apologize if they need to,
and let the moms clear the air. That's all.

774
00:46:40,955 --> 00:46:42,424
- That's right.
- Yeah.

775
00:46:42,424 --> 00:46:44,355
Right.

776
00:46:44,355 --> 00:46:46,692
Oh, the drinks are here.

777
00:46:50,743 --> 00:46:52,443
Thank you.

778
00:46:53,807 --> 00:46:56,375
Oh, you made it?

779
00:46:56,375 --> 00:46:58,392
Sorry I'm late.

780
00:47:00,155 --> 00:47:02,123
Just a second.

781
00:47:02,123 --> 00:47:05,359
Oh, I saw some blood earlier,
and I'm still feeling queasy.

782
00:47:14,526 --> 00:47:16,411
Hye Ri's mom is...

783
00:47:16,411 --> 00:47:18,151
- Over here.
- Here.

784
00:47:18,151 --> 00:47:20,403
Oh, there you are.

785
00:47:20,403 --> 00:47:24,192
Hye Ri's mom, I heard
our Seo Jun pushed Hye Ri.

786
00:47:24,192 --> 00:47:27,199
That little punk.

787
00:47:27,199 --> 00:47:30,871
I'll give him a good talking-to
when I get home.

788
00:47:30,871 --> 00:47:33,043
I'll make him write an apology letter too.

789
00:47:33,043 --> 00:47:36,159
But I heard he already apologized to Hye Ri.

790
00:47:36,763 --> 00:47:38,315
Yes, he did.

791
00:47:38,315 --> 00:47:41,127
Yes, he apologized.

792
00:47:41,127 --> 00:47:42,959
Well, that's good.

793
00:47:44,535 --> 00:47:46,816
I'll apologize too, on behalf of his mom.

794
00:47:46,816 --> 00:47:49,226
- Well...
- I'm sorry, Hye Ri's mom.

795
00:47:50,255 --> 00:47:52,026
Wow!

796
00:47:52,026 --> 00:47:55,526
That's a bold apology.

797
00:48:01,137 --> 00:48:02,837
I...

798
00:48:05,519 --> 00:48:07,219
Sor...

799
00:48:08,571 --> 00:48:10,263
What should I do?

800
00:48:10,263 --> 00:48:13,292
Do you think Yul will be okay
without going to the hospital?

801
00:48:15,999 --> 00:48:19,583
Oh, it went down pretty quickly
after I put some medicine on it.

802
00:48:19,583 --> 00:48:20,991
Thanks for asking.

803
00:48:20,991 --> 00:48:23,592
- Oh, good.
- What a relief.

804
00:48:24,731 --> 00:48:26,943
Wow, this is great, right?

805
00:48:26,943 --> 00:48:30,599
Let's have a proper drink
and loosen up. Cheers.

806
00:48:30,599 --> 00:48:32,343
- Out of drinks.
- Oh, no beer.

807
00:48:32,343 --> 00:48:33,715
Can I have a glass of beer?

808
00:48:33,715 --> 00:48:36,592
- Here, you can have some of mine for now.
- Okay, sure.

809
00:48:39,619 --> 00:48:41,227
Cheers.

810
00:48:41,227 --> 00:48:43,559
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

811
00:48:50,962 --> 00:48:52,343
Well...

812
00:48:52,343 --> 00:48:56,919
Assistant Manager Ki,
did I happen to do something wrong?

813
00:48:56,919 --> 00:48:58,619
Not at all.

814
00:48:59,475 --> 00:49:03,899
You just seem pretty different from
how you were at the restaurant.

815
00:49:03,899 --> 00:49:06,303
You haven't said much at all.

816
00:49:06,303 --> 00:49:08,971
This is the real me.
Earlier, I was putting on an act.

817
00:49:08,971 --> 00:49:11,543
Why would you do that?

818
00:49:11,543 --> 00:49:12,603
Do you like me?

819
00:49:12,603 --> 00:49:14,559
Yeah, I mean, no.

820
00:49:19,307 --> 00:49:20,643
Yeah.

821
00:49:20,643 --> 00:49:23,471
I'm sorry, but I have no interest in you.

822
00:49:23,471 --> 00:49:25,326
You're not my type.

823
00:49:26,155 --> 00:49:28,231
I'm sorry for asking you out.

824
00:49:28,231 --> 00:49:30,231
It was way too impulsive.

825
00:49:30,231 --> 00:49:32,119
Sorry.

826
00:49:32,119 --> 00:49:34,859
That's what I wanted to tell you,
so I asked to see you today.

827
00:49:38,027 --> 00:49:42,167
Then what is your type?

828
00:49:42,167 --> 00:49:43,867
I'm...

829
00:49:46,579 --> 00:49:49,659
attracted to a woman strong enough
to hold my life in her hands.

830
00:49:49,659 --> 00:49:51,375
Eat up and relax, rookie.

831
00:49:51,375 --> 00:49:53,783
A woman who could hurt me at any time,

832
00:49:53,783 --> 00:49:55,659
but chooses not to.

833
00:49:57,892 --> 00:50:01,192
That's quite a unique preference.

834
00:50:04,347 --> 00:50:08,131
But Assistant Manager Ki,
you don't even know me.

835
00:50:08,131 --> 00:50:10,103
That's right.

836
00:50:10,103 --> 00:50:12,426
And I don't particularly want to know you.

837
00:50:17,559 --> 00:50:19,191
Okay!

838
00:50:19,191 --> 00:50:21,992
Found today's punching bag.

839
00:50:21,992 --> 00:50:23,992
- Found one.
- Found one.

840
00:50:30,392 --> 00:50:32,692
[Cybercrime Unit, Sergeant Kim]

841
00:50:35,667 --> 00:50:37,931
- Yes, Mr. Kim.
- Hey, Mr. Beom. It's me.

842
00:50:37,931 --> 00:50:39,575
Guess what I found?

843
00:50:39,575 --> 00:50:40,992
I sent you a link.
Can you check it right away?

844
00:50:40,992 --> 00:50:43,692
Sure. Give me a second.

845
00:50:48,683 --> 00:50:50,926
Hello, gentlemen!

846
00:50:50,926 --> 00:50:53,626
- It's time for Mace Man's justice.
- Justice!

847
00:50:53,626 --> 00:50:56,607
Let's get things started with a bang.

848
00:50:56,607 --> 00:50:57,607
What's this?

849
00:50:57,607 --> 00:50:59,992
Apparently, it's a streaming site
that's been growing underground lately.

850
00:50:59,992 --> 00:51:02,755
They livestream violent or obscene videos,

851
00:51:02,755 --> 00:51:04,199
and apparently get paid in
some kind of cryptocurrency.

852
00:51:04,199 --> 00:51:08,779
Who are we going to teach a lesson today?

853
00:51:08,779 --> 00:51:10,359
Let's go with a pretty one, if possible.

854
00:51:10,359 --> 00:51:12,599
You won't be able to see their faces
once they're covered in blood, idiot.

855
00:51:12,599 --> 00:51:14,631
See them? Three masked men.

856
00:51:14,631 --> 00:51:17,779
These guys look like the couple-assault
suspects you've been after, right?

857
00:51:17,779 --> 00:51:20,359
Oh, you're right.

858
00:51:20,359 --> 00:51:23,475
Man, so cryptocurrency was their motive?

859
00:51:23,475 --> 00:51:24,683
Does it show where they are?

860
00:51:24,683 --> 00:51:25,967
It says Songju Park.

861
00:51:25,967 --> 00:51:27,263
Songju Park?

862
00:51:27,263 --> 00:51:28,792
Huh? That's nearby.

863
00:51:28,792 --> 00:51:32,087
So what do you think of
these punks, gentlemen?

864
00:51:32,087 --> 00:51:34,592
Zoom in on the woman's face.

865
00:51:34,592 --> 00:51:37,115
Let's see.

866
00:51:37,115 --> 00:51:39,327
- Huh?
- There.

867
00:51:39,327 --> 00:51:40,483
Darn it.

868
00:51:40,483 --> 00:51:42,183
Ah, well...

869
00:51:43,047 --> 00:51:45,739
Mr. Kim, please call for backup
from the local precinct,

870
00:51:45,739 --> 00:51:47,226
and send ambulances to Songju Park.

871
00:51:47,226 --> 00:51:48,695
- Three ambulances.
- Three?

872
00:51:48,695 --> 00:51:52,291
- Not two?
- No, three. Make sure it's three.

873
00:51:52,291 --> 00:51:55,447
No. Kwon Se Ah, please!

874
00:51:55,447 --> 00:51:57,147
This way, right?

875
00:51:57,767 --> 00:51:59,475
What are they doing?

876
00:51:59,475 --> 00:52:01,035
Why are they just walking?

877
00:52:01,035 --> 00:52:03,747
The guy's obviously a pathetic loser.

878
00:52:03,747 --> 00:52:06,215
He can't even hold her hand.

879
00:52:06,215 --> 00:52:12,092
Well, gentlemen,
I think it's time to teach them a lesson.

880
00:52:14,355 --> 00:52:15,820
I've already been rejected,

881
00:52:15,820 --> 00:52:18,692
but since I started this confession anyway,
let me just finish it.

882
00:52:19,987 --> 00:52:24,967
The first day we met,
when you said you'd help me find Yul,

883
00:52:24,967 --> 00:52:29,495
that's when you dove straight into my heart.

884
00:52:29,495 --> 00:52:31,195
And...

885
00:52:33,563 --> 00:52:35,263
Who on earth are you?

886
00:52:36,587 --> 00:52:38,287
Wait...

887
00:52:40,631 --> 00:52:43,059
Assistant Manager Ki, are you okay?

888
00:52:45,439 --> 00:52:47,259
I'm...

889
00:52:47,259 --> 00:52:50,619
attracted to a woman strong enough
to hold my life in her hands.

890
00:52:50,619 --> 00:52:53,643
A woman who could hurt me at any time,

891
00:52:53,643 --> 00:52:54,826
but chooses not to.

892
00:52:54,826 --> 00:52:57,512
[Kwon Se Ah, Current: Graduate student,
College of Physical Education]

893
00:52:57,512 --> 00:52:59,403
[Former: Women's Judo National Team Reserve]

894
00:52:59,403 --> 00:53:00,731
Kwon Se Ah, please.

895
00:53:00,731 --> 00:53:04,192
Take it easy. Don't kill them.

896
00:53:07,075 --> 00:53:08,826
Assistant Manager Ki!

897
00:53:08,826 --> 00:53:12,635
Yeah, I'm... I'm fine.

898
00:53:12,635 --> 00:53:14,059
Oh, no, what do I do?

899
00:53:14,059 --> 00:53:16,759
I'm sorry. Are you okay?

900
00:53:16,759 --> 00:53:18,331
Oh, dear.

901
00:53:18,331 --> 00:53:20,475
Oh, please don't come any closer.

902
00:53:20,475 --> 00:53:23,559
Please, just stay back.

903
00:53:26,272 --> 00:53:29,492
Oh, my tailbone... Oh...

904
00:53:29,492 --> 00:53:32,343
Jeez, I said stay back.

905
00:53:32,343 --> 00:53:34,826
Oh, my, are you okay?

906
00:53:34,826 --> 00:53:36,419
Oh...

907
00:53:36,419 --> 00:53:38,692
Stay still! Don't move!

908
00:53:38,692 --> 00:53:40,563
Darn, this is so embarrassing.

909
00:53:40,563 --> 00:53:42,555
Hey, take out that punk first!

910
00:53:42,555 --> 00:53:45,292
If you keep doing this,
I'm seriously going to call the police...

911
00:53:53,439 --> 00:53:55,859
No time for that.

912
00:53:57,863 --> 00:54:00,171
Oh, I'm terrified.

913
00:54:00,171 --> 00:54:03,492
Assistant Manager Ki,
that must've scared you, right?

914
00:54:06,892 --> 00:54:09,426
It... did.

915
00:54:10,531 --> 00:54:11,879
They just came out of nowhere.

916
00:54:11,879 --> 00:54:13,159
Hey, Kwon Se Ah!

917
00:54:13,159 --> 00:54:14,159
Huh? What?

918
00:54:14,159 --> 00:54:15,419
Hey, you!

919
00:54:15,419 --> 00:54:17,439
You...

920
00:54:17,439 --> 00:54:19,067
I knew you'd pull something like this.

921
00:54:19,067 --> 00:54:20,639
Huh?

922
00:54:20,639 --> 00:54:22,263
Hey!

923
00:54:22,263 --> 00:54:25,039
Hey, look at what you've done to him...

924
00:54:25,039 --> 00:54:27,822
I told you not to use
your techniques carelessly, right?

925
00:54:27,822 --> 00:54:30,883
Well... It just happened automatically.

926
00:54:30,883 --> 00:54:33,239
Hey, wake up!

927
00:54:33,239 --> 00:54:36,383
Are you okay? Hey!

928
00:54:36,383 --> 00:54:39,391
Wow, he passed out cold.

929
00:54:39,391 --> 00:54:41,679
Okay, no visible injuries.

930
00:54:41,679 --> 00:54:43,427
And you're not hurt anywhere, right?
Of course not.

931
00:54:43,427 --> 00:54:45,455
- Yeah.
- And you...

932
00:54:45,455 --> 00:54:48,259
barely had to lift a finger anyway.

933
00:54:58,319 --> 00:55:00,759
Oh, nice timing.

934
00:55:02,192 --> 00:55:04,192
[Beom Seong Hun, Current:
Nambu Station's Youngest Detective]

935
00:55:04,192 --> 00:55:06,192
[Former: Asian Games Gold Medalist
in Men's Judo, Special Police Hire]

936
00:55:06,192 --> 00:55:07,719
Don't move.

937
00:55:07,719 --> 00:55:12,555
You're under arrest for aggravated assault
and obstruction of official duties.

938
00:55:12,555 --> 00:55:16,375
You have the right
to remain silent and to an attorney.

939
00:55:16,375 --> 00:55:18,759
Oh, right. And anything stupid you say
can be used against you,

940
00:55:18,759 --> 00:55:20,759
so watch what you say.

941
00:55:22,392 --> 00:55:25,559
Mr. Tiger! True colors of a cop!
Champions of justice!

942
00:55:25,559 --> 00:55:26,819
- Hey!
- Hey!

943
00:55:26,819 --> 00:55:29,826
- Take them down and finish it!
- Take them down and finish it!

944
00:55:29,826 --> 00:55:31,292
- You remember?
- Hey, how do you know that?

945
00:55:31,292 --> 00:55:33,699
- This is nothing.
- Hey, what's going on here?

946
00:55:33,699 --> 00:55:35,647
- A throw.
- Hey, that's not right!

947
00:55:35,647 --> 00:55:37,451
No, you do it from here, like this!

948
00:55:37,451 --> 00:55:38,692
- Bam!
- Oh!

949
00:55:38,692 --> 00:55:41,835
What was that? Wow, you're good.

950
00:55:41,835 --> 00:55:44,347
- Of course, I'm a cop.
- Jeez.

951
00:55:44,347 --> 00:55:46,792
The police will be here soon...

952
00:55:49,007 --> 00:55:50,707
The kid...

953
00:55:51,407 --> 00:55:54,287
She's getting harder and harder to handle.

954
00:55:54,287 --> 00:55:58,007
Of course. The older they get,
the less they listen.

955
00:55:58,007 --> 00:56:01,655
I complained to my mom once,
and you know what she said?

956
00:56:01,655 --> 00:56:03,083
Did she say she'd scold your kid?

957
00:56:03,083 --> 00:56:05,992
She said my kid's
exactly like I was as a kid.

958
00:56:07,391 --> 00:56:10,826
She prayed for me
to have a daughter just like me,

959
00:56:12,091 --> 00:56:14,667
and her wish came true.

960
00:56:14,667 --> 00:56:16,759
That scared me more than anything.

961
00:56:16,759 --> 00:56:18,903
"A daughter who takes after me."

962
00:56:18,903 --> 00:56:22,407
Kids are half born that way
and half learn by watching.

963
00:56:22,407 --> 00:56:27,219
That's why they say,
"A child is a reflection of their parents."

964
00:56:27,219 --> 00:56:30,415
That saying, that one really hits me hard.

965
00:56:30,415 --> 00:56:33,175
I mean, isn't that a little unfair to me?

966
00:56:33,175 --> 00:56:38,359
All the time and effort I put into her...

967
00:56:40,039 --> 00:56:42,103
Jeez.

968
00:56:42,103 --> 00:56:43,431
Hold on.

969
00:56:43,431 --> 00:56:46,063
- It's your husband.
- Your husband.

970
00:56:46,063 --> 00:56:47,763
What?

971
00:56:48,559 --> 00:56:50,526
What time is it right now?

972
00:56:50,526 --> 00:56:52,967
Look at the clock.

973
00:56:52,967 --> 00:56:55,763
You come home at midnight every day,

974
00:56:55,763 --> 00:57:00,127
and you're complaining about
having to watch the kid one day early?

975
00:57:00,127 --> 00:57:01,559
What, her bath?

976
00:57:01,559 --> 00:57:05,247
Just give her a bath yourself.

977
00:57:05,247 --> 00:57:08,559
I don't know. Just put her to bed.

978
00:57:09,535 --> 00:57:11,459
Or whatever.

979
00:57:12,179 --> 00:57:15,615
Seriously, how is he exactly like my husband?

980
00:57:15,615 --> 00:57:17,059
We had this kid together,

981
00:57:17,059 --> 00:57:21,439
so why am I the one expected to do
all the parenting?

982
00:57:21,439 --> 00:57:22,819
If this is how it's going to be,

983
00:57:22,819 --> 00:57:24,611
he shouldn't have been begging
for a second kid.

984
00:57:24,611 --> 00:57:26,383
Well, my husband,

985
00:57:26,383 --> 00:57:29,755
even when I beg him to play
with the kids instead of drinking,

986
00:57:29,755 --> 00:57:32,199
all he ever says is, "Yeah, yeah."

987
00:57:32,199 --> 00:57:33,992
And one time,

988
00:57:34,923 --> 00:57:36,552
he called saying he was leaving,

989
00:57:36,552 --> 00:57:38,119
and then he took so long to show up
that I went down to check,

990
00:57:38,119 --> 00:57:41,126
and there he was, sleeping
in the parking lot. This guy, seriously.

991
00:57:41,126 --> 00:57:42,126
In the car?

992
00:57:42,126 --> 00:57:43,451
Yeah.

993
00:57:43,451 --> 00:57:44,971
What a gentleman.

994
00:57:44,971 --> 00:57:46,147
What?

995
00:57:46,147 --> 00:57:49,163
I got a call from the security office
once about Hye Ri's dad.

996
00:57:49,163 --> 00:57:51,326
They said he was snoring
away in the elevator.

997
00:57:51,326 --> 00:57:52,359
Oh, God.

998
00:57:52,359 --> 00:57:55,826
What if the kids learn from watching them?

999
00:57:56,831 --> 00:58:00,059
Then just raise them alone as I do.

1000
00:58:07,315 --> 00:58:08,867
What about you, Yul's mom?

1001
00:58:08,867 --> 00:58:10,663
What?

1002
00:58:10,663 --> 00:58:12,275
Yul's dad.

1003
00:58:12,275 --> 00:58:14,383
I'm curious what kind of dad Yul has.

1004
00:58:14,383 --> 00:58:17,292
Yeah, me too. What's he like?

1005
00:58:18,771 --> 00:58:20,792
My husband?

1006
00:58:26,363 --> 00:58:28,011
Did my little girl get hurt a lot?

1007
00:58:28,011 --> 00:58:30,703
Yeah, it hurt a lot.

1008
00:58:30,703 --> 00:58:35,455
It's okay. I put some medicine on it,
so it'll get better soon.

1009
00:58:35,455 --> 00:58:39,092
What made you the saddest today, Yul?

1010
00:58:40,619 --> 00:58:42,459
Hye Ri cried today.

1011
00:58:42,459 --> 00:58:45,079
Oh, did seeing Hye Ri cry
make you the saddest?

1012
00:58:45,079 --> 00:58:48,271
- Yeah.
- Why did that make you so sad?

1013
00:58:48,271 --> 00:58:53,559
Because Mommy told me
to get along with my friends.

1014
00:58:53,559 --> 00:58:58,391
Oh, you wanted to get along
with your friend, but it didn't work out?

1015
00:58:58,391 --> 00:59:02,047
Yeah. But we shouldn't hurt our friends.

1016
00:59:02,047 --> 00:59:04,147
That's right. We shouldn't hurt our friends.

1017
00:59:04,147 --> 00:59:08,347
- No biting and no pushing, right?
- Yeah.

1018
00:59:08,347 --> 00:59:12,697
But sometimes things like that happen
when you're playing with friends.

1019
00:59:12,697 --> 00:59:13,923
What should you do then?

1020
00:59:13,923 --> 00:59:15,535
I should say "Sorry."

1021
00:59:15,535 --> 00:59:16,535
That's right.

1022
00:59:16,535 --> 00:59:20,815
Apologize, make up, and be friends again.

1023
00:59:20,815 --> 00:59:23,531
Yeah, I'll give them presents
and ask them to play with me.

1024
00:59:23,531 --> 00:59:26,275
Wow, your friends are going to love that.

1025
00:59:26,275 --> 00:59:29,923
Then how about we pick out presents
for your friends together tomorrow?

1026
00:59:29,923 --> 00:59:31,359
- Yeah.
- Good.

1027
00:59:31,359 --> 00:59:33,799
Now, what should we play?

1028
00:59:33,799 --> 00:59:34,859
Superman?

1029
00:59:34,859 --> 00:59:36,483
Alright, arms out! Superman!

1030
00:59:36,483 --> 00:59:38,326
Stretch!

1031
00:59:38,326 --> 00:59:40,259
Wow!

1032
00:59:43,927 --> 00:59:46,351
They say the one who throws the punch
sleeps like a baby.

1033
00:59:46,351 --> 00:59:50,026
Even the punk who threatened the chief
seems pretty darn comfortable.

1034
00:59:51,991 --> 00:59:54,126
Hey, Lee Dong Jin, wake up.

1035
00:59:55,539 --> 00:59:57,359
Wake up, now!

1036
01:00:00,039 --> 01:00:02,650
God, because of you,
I made a total fool of myself

1037
01:00:02,650 --> 01:00:04,607
in front of the commissioner today...

1038
01:00:04,607 --> 01:00:07,759
God, why did I ever bring in
a blockhead like you?

1039
01:00:07,759 --> 01:00:09,383
You...

1040
01:00:09,383 --> 01:00:11,595
You have to risk your life.

1041
01:00:11,595 --> 01:00:13,792
Otherwise, we're both going down.

1042
01:00:13,792 --> 01:00:14,807
What?

1043
01:00:14,807 --> 01:00:16,283
What are you doing?

1044
01:00:16,283 --> 01:00:18,692
Move it and pack your stuff, you punk!

1045
01:00:25,892 --> 01:00:28,711
♪ Every day on the bus to school ♪

1046
01:00:28,711 --> 01:00:32,159
♪ I like the girl
who always sits in the same seat ♪

1047
01:00:32,159 --> 01:00:35,579
♪ I sometimes deliberately stand beside her ♪

1048
01:00:35,579 --> 01:00:38,959
♪ But somehow I feel like
I'm not good enough ♪

1049
01:00:38,959 --> 01:00:42,292
♪ No, I'm fine. Don't worry about it ♪

1050
01:00:42,292 --> 01:00:45,726
- ♪ I don't have a boyfriend now ♪
- Come on out.

1051
01:00:45,726 --> 01:00:50,043
♪ But why won't you say a word? ♪

1052
01:00:50,043 --> 01:00:53,292
♪ I know you really need me ♪

1053
01:00:53,292 --> 01:00:57,892
♪ You're too idealistic,
no woman is going to approach you ♪

1054
01:00:57,892 --> 01:01:02,635
♪ No woman is ever going
to make the first move ♪

1055
01:01:02,635 --> 01:01:08,192
♪ I'm no different, you know ♪

1056
01:01:14,092 --> 01:01:17,026
♪ Hesitating over something so simple ♪

1057
01:01:17,026 --> 01:01:21,026
♪ Watching you be so hopelessly
hesitant drives me crazy ♪

1058
01:01:21,026 --> 01:01:25,092
♪ You're too idealistic,
no woman is going to approach you ♪

1059
01:01:25,092 --> 01:01:30,263
♪ No woman is ever going
to make the first move ♪

1060
01:01:30,263 --> 01:01:35,492
♪ I'm no different, you know ♪

1061
01:01:43,403 --> 01:01:46,459
I used to be better at this.

1062
01:01:48,792 --> 01:01:50,179
Yul's mom, sing one too.

1063
01:01:50,179 --> 01:01:51,792
- Oh, this is so much fun.
- Sing a song.

1064
01:01:51,792 --> 01:01:52,826
- Come on, sing.
- Me?

1065
01:01:52,826 --> 01:01:53,826
- No, I can't.
- We can't be the only ones singing.

1066
01:01:53,826 --> 01:01:54,826
- A song?
- Sing one!

1067
01:01:54,826 --> 01:01:59,092
- Sing a song!
- Sing a song!

1068
01:01:59,092 --> 01:02:03,926
[A Million Roses]

1069
01:02:08,091 --> 01:02:12,692
♪ Long ago, from some distant star ♪

1070
01:02:13,492 --> 01:02:19,359
♪ When I came into this world ♪

1071
01:02:19,359 --> 01:02:25,243
♪ I heard a small voice ♪

1072
01:02:25,243 --> 01:02:31,035
♪ Telling me to come give love ♪

1073
01:02:31,035 --> 01:02:34,435
♪ That only blooms when you love ♪

1074
01:02:34,435 --> 01:02:36,879
She's surprisingly romantic.

1075
01:02:36,879 --> 01:02:38,792
Exactly.

1076
01:02:38,792 --> 01:02:42,079
Why is she singing such a gloomy song?

1077
01:02:42,079 --> 01:02:44,692
She's killing the mood.

1078
01:02:44,692 --> 01:02:48,627
She's quite something.

1079
01:02:48,627 --> 01:02:54,415
♪ Roses of love in bloom ♪

1080
01:02:54,415 --> 01:03:00,131
♪ Without a heart full of hate ♪

1081
01:03:00,131 --> 01:03:06,091
♪ When you give love without holding back ♪

1082
01:03:06,091 --> 01:03:11,959
♪ Millions and millions of roses bloom ♪

1083
01:03:11,959 --> 01:03:17,871
♪ And I can return to
our beautiful, beloved star ♪

1084
01:03:17,871 --> 01:03:23,723
♪ Without a heart full of hate ♪

1085
01:03:23,723 --> 01:03:28,892
♪ When you give love without holding back ♪

1086
01:03:29,503 --> 01:03:35,367
♪ Millions and millions of roses bloom ♪

1087
01:03:35,367 --> 01:03:40,426
♪ And I can return to
our beautiful, beloved star ♪

1088
01:03:44,179 --> 01:03:47,263
A special task force has been formed

1089
01:03:47,263 --> 01:03:50,443
to apprehend the serial killer
known as Kingfisher.

1090
01:03:50,443 --> 01:03:52,848
Accordingly, the scattered
investigative information and personnel

1091
01:03:52,848 --> 01:03:54,935
from each case
are expected to be consolidated,

1092
01:03:54,935 --> 01:04:00,126
with dedicated staff assigned
to accelerate the Kingfisher investigation.

1093
01:04:31,126 --> 01:04:33,359
[Ok's Flower Shop]

1094
01:04:33,359 --> 01:04:40,259
[Ok's Flower Shop]

1095
01:04:49,159 --> 01:04:52,592
Will this finally end with
Kingfisher's arrest?

1096
01:04:52,592 --> 01:04:57,359
Attention is now focused on
the newly formed Kingfisher task force.

1097
01:06:00,303 --> 01:06:02,392
The mugging during the World Cup?

1098
01:06:02,392 --> 01:06:05,892
I believe it could provide a clue
to Kingfisher's identity.

1099
01:06:05,892 --> 01:06:07,763
Do you remember the caller's voice?

1100
01:06:07,763 --> 01:06:09,539
The message on the first card
they sent was...

1101
01:06:09,539 --> 01:06:11,983
"I hope you find your own beautiful scenery."

1102
01:06:11,983 --> 01:06:14,226
Can you tell me anything
about the person sending the flowers?

1103
01:06:14,226 --> 01:06:16,126
Who is it? The person you saw that day.

1104
01:06:16,126 --> 01:06:17,126
Some woman.

1105
01:06:17,126 --> 01:06:18,771
Why are you looking for that woman?

1106
01:06:18,771 --> 01:06:21,579
She either witnessed Kingfisher,
or she is Kingfisher.

1107
01:06:21,579 --> 01:06:23,692
You should still have
the voice message on your phone.

1108
01:06:23,692 --> 01:06:24,692
Who's taking this case?

1109
01:06:24,692 --> 01:06:28,303
We'll set a trap around Gu Jung Yeol
before Kingfisher makes a move.

1110
01:06:28,303 --> 01:06:29,926
Client meeting starts.

1111
01:06:29,926 --> 01:06:32,526
Let's go catch Kingfisher.
